<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Panormus</h1><p class="st-meta">734 BCE – 254 BCE (approx.) · capital Panormus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Phoenician and Punic city on the bay of Palermo, Carthage's chief stronghold in western Sicily until Rome captured it in 254 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a> settled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Panormus</a>, called Ziz ('flower') on its coins, on a promontory between two river inlets by the late 8th or 7th century BCE. Its deep natural harbour gave it the Greek name Panormos, 'all-harbour'. With <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/motya">Motya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solunto">Soloeis</a> it formed the cluster of Phoenician towns in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> that came under Carthaginian protection.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Panormus</a> prospered from trade between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> and the Greek and Elymian towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and served as a key Carthaginian military base: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamilcar-i-of-carthage">Hamilcar</a> landed there before the battle of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/himera">Himera</a> in 480 BCE. Its necropolis shows a mixed population of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phoenicians">Phoenicians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elymians">Elymians</a>. It minted coins with Punic and Greek legends and was ruled by local magistrates under Carthaginian oversight.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-punic-war">First Punic War</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palermo">Panormus</a> in 254 BCE, and in 250 BCE the consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-caecilius-metellus-consul-251-bce">Lucius Caecilius Metellus</a> defeated a Carthaginian army with elephants beneath its walls. The city became a free town of the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and later grew into Palermo, capital of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-sicily">Emirate of Sicily</a> and the Norman kingdom.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 734 BCE – 254 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.09%;width:9.55%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>734 BCE – 254 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Panormus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Phoenician religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Phoenician</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ziz, Palermo (ancient)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-494&amp;focus=panormus" aria-label="Panormus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5013 808 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Panormus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5333 1064L5259 1106M5333 1064L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5259 1106h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5333 1064h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5333 1064h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Panormus. <a href="/atlas?year=-494&amp;focu